1
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:38,719
I'll translate that sentence again.

2
00:01:39,079 --> 00:01:40,000
In the future,

3
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:42,480
computer science will be

4
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:44,680
a skill that everyone
has a good command of.

5
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:47,560
In the future, computer science

6
00:01:47,719 --> 00:01:50,120
will be a skill
that everyone has a good command of.

7
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,480
Memorize every example sentence.

8
00:01:52,719 --> 00:01:53,599
I'll be checking tomorrow.

9
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,239
(As I remember it,)

10
00:02:00,239 --> 00:02:01,280
(this city)

11
00:02:01,959 --> 00:02:03,920
(was always shrouded in gloom.)

12
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:09,919
(May 1994)

13
00:02:09,919 --> 00:02:12,360
(Smoke from the industrial stacks)

14
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,719
(made the entire city)

15
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,439
(look gray and hazy.)

16
00:02:19,879 --> 00:02:21,520
(Back then, I felt)

17
00:02:22,639 --> 00:02:23,800
(that living here)

18
00:02:25,439 --> 00:02:29,080
(made everything bleak and futile.)

19
00:02:42,039 --> 00:02:42,960
(That gloom)

20
00:02:43,759 --> 00:02:45,879
(covered every corner of my world.)

21
00:02:47,639 --> 00:02:49,039
(Like a sky choked by clouds,)

22
00:02:49,719 --> 00:02:51,240
(the roar of giant machines,)

23
00:02:52,039 --> 00:02:53,719
(a room reeking of sweat,)

24
00:02:55,039 --> 00:02:56,919
(and the stench of a sewer.)

25
00:02:57,759 --> 00:02:58,919
(It filled my eyes,)

26
00:02:59,639 --> 00:03:00,080
(ears,)

27
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,199
(mouth,)

28
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:02,319
(nose,)

29
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:04,199
(and heart.)

30
00:03:16,319 --> 00:03:17,240
Five-two-zero.

31
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,039
(Public Telephone)

32
00:03:18,039 --> 00:03:19,240
Lei, get the phone!

33
00:03:20,009 --> 00:03:20,930
- Hurry!
- Coming!

34
00:03:22,879 --> 00:03:23,639
(Back then,)

35
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,280
(Dad supported us with odd jobs)

36
00:03:26,719 --> 00:03:27,879
(at construction sites.)

37
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:31,400
(Mom took in laundry to help.)

38
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,479
(So our home)

39
00:03:33,479 --> 00:03:35,159
(was always piled with laundry.)

40
00:03:53,744 --> 00:03:57,776
=Ren Yu=

41
00:03:59,669 --> 00:04:02,526
=Episode 1=

42
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:17,759
You're back.

43
00:04:17,879 --> 00:04:18,600
Dinner's ready.

44
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:38,519
Don't dawdle.

45
00:04:38,519 --> 00:04:39,720
Come eat.

46
00:04:39,759 --> 00:04:40,480
Clear that up.

47
00:04:41,439 --> 00:04:42,639
Su Zhe, dinner!

48
00:04:57,879 --> 00:04:59,040
You're too close to the TV.

49
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,439
You'll ruin your eyes.

50
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:02,399
Any farther and I'll be by the couch.

51
00:05:06,199 --> 00:05:06,680
Sit there.

52
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:12,360
Let him eat.

53
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,360
You've spoiled him.

54
00:05:13,959 --> 00:05:14,839
You're blaming me?

55
00:05:14,959 --> 00:05:16,319
He hasn't watched TV in two days.

56
00:05:16,319 --> 00:05:17,800
The poor kid's going stir-crazy.

57
00:05:17,959 --> 00:05:19,959
We couldn't even pay the electric bill.

58
00:05:22,639 --> 00:05:23,639
Ten years raising you,

59
00:05:23,639 --> 00:05:26,279
and all you do is eat and play.

60
00:05:26,399 --> 00:05:27,759
I can't even go outside.

61
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:35,120
The bill's paid now.

62
00:05:35,279 --> 00:05:36,279
Go watch TV.

63
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,120
Su Zhe.

64
00:05:40,399 --> 00:05:41,319
Enough food?

65
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,120
I'll give you more.

66
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,360
I noticed some old things

67
00:05:57,879 --> 00:05:59,199
were sold today.

68
00:05:59,639 --> 00:06:00,879
How else could we pay the bill?

69
00:06:01,399 --> 00:06:01,959
Just a few.

70
00:06:01,959 --> 00:06:03,959
Your dad's worn-out clothes.

71
00:06:03,959 --> 00:06:04,879
They were worn out.

72
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:05,920
And your textbooks.

73
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:07,399
Your brother had used them.

74
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,480
I had an old pencil case, too.

75
00:06:10,519 --> 00:06:12,000
Right. We sold that, too.

76
00:06:14,519 --> 00:06:16,120
There were seven or eight yuan inside.

77
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:17,079
Did you

78
00:06:17,079 --> 00:06:18,680
leave that in there?

79
00:06:18,879 --> 00:06:19,920
It was a lifesaver.

80
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:21,879
Those were my savings.

81
00:06:22,879 --> 00:06:24,279
My girl's grown up.

82
00:06:24,279 --> 00:06:26,839
You know how to save now.

83
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:35,240
I was saving for English tapes.

84
00:06:37,399 --> 00:06:38,439
You call that saving?

85
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,759
You stole it from me.

86
00:06:41,439 --> 00:06:42,240
Think I don't know

87
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,279
what you're planning?

88
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,680
Hiding away money,

89
00:06:45,519 --> 00:06:46,800
planning to go to college?

90
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,519
Right?

91
00:06:48,639 --> 00:06:50,839
Stop dreaming about the impossible.

92
00:06:51,639 --> 00:06:52,600
Work after graduation.

93
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,199
Make money.

94
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,399
Pay the fine off soon,

95
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:58,360
so your brother can attend school.

96
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,160
I want to go to college.

97
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:04,199
Do you know how hard that is?

98
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:07,000
Is college something

99
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,040
like us can dream of?

100
00:07:10,199 --> 00:07:10,560
I...

101
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,240
Stop it.

102
00:07:11,759 --> 00:07:13,079
It's always about yourself.

103
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:16,600
How did you get so selfish?

104
00:07:29,319 --> 00:07:30,040
I'm full.

105
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:51,000
(English Alphabet)

106
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,120
Su Zhe.

107
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:07,600
Su Zhe.

108
00:08:08,579 --> 00:08:10,480
I'll leave the laundry over there.

109
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:11,560
I'll hang it later.

110
00:08:12,079 --> 00:08:12,439
Okay.

111
00:08:14,959 --> 00:08:15,600
Like it?

112
00:08:18,639 --> 00:08:20,160
This one's my favorite.

113
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:27,360
Looks good, right?

114
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,000
It does.

115
00:08:31,519 --> 00:08:32,879
It looks amazing.

116
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:34,279
So cool.

117
00:08:34,559 --> 00:08:35,240
Try this.

118
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:36,440
A zipper, too.

119
00:08:40,279 --> 00:08:41,240
Dad, how do I look?

120
00:08:41,759 --> 00:08:42,639
Fits you perfectly.

121
00:08:43,759 --> 00:08:44,639
I love it!

122
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:48,840
Turn around.

123
00:09:28,159 --> 00:09:30,440
(I was saving for English tapes.)

124
00:09:31,399 --> 00:09:32,360
(Hiding away money,)

125
00:09:32,759 --> 00:09:34,039
(planning to go to college?)

126
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:37,399
(Stop dreaming about the impossible.)

127
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,000
(Some people are alive,)

128
00:09:48,279 --> 00:09:49,480
(yet they're already dead.)

129
00:09:51,279 --> 00:09:53,039
(That's how I often felt.)

130
00:09:54,759 --> 00:09:56,039
(Throughout my adolescence,)

131
00:09:56,039 --> 00:09:57,799
(I moved through life like a corpse.)

132
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,159
(Then I heard about)

133
00:10:00,159 --> 00:10:01,720
(the English recitation contest.)

134
00:10:03,639 --> 00:10:04,360
(I knew)

135
00:10:05,879 --> 00:10:07,679
(this was my chance to come alive.)

136
00:10:10,519 --> 00:10:11,440
She knew

137
00:10:11,879 --> 00:10:17,480
this was her last evening
she could ever see the prince,

138
00:10:18,279 --> 00:10:19,120
for whom

139
00:10:19,519 --> 00:10:23,799
she had forsaken
her kindred and her home.

140
00:10:24,519 --> 00:10:27,679
She had given up her beautiful voice

141
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:32,159
and suffered unheard-of pain daily.

142
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:33,159
Let me see it.

143
00:10:33,159 --> 00:10:33,600
While

144
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:39,159
he knew nothing of it.

145
00:10:41,639 --> 00:10:42,080
Ma Na.

146
00:10:42,639 --> 00:10:44,559
What did I just read?

147
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:45,960
What was it?

148
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,120
Far out at sea,

149
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,440
the water is as blue

150
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:56,080
as the loveliest cornflower petals,

151
00:10:56,679 --> 00:10:58,679
and as clear

152
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,399
as the purest...

153
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,480
That's the story's first sentence.

154
00:11:04,159 --> 00:11:06,399
I read a passage from later on.

155
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:08,240
Study it properly at home.

156
00:11:08,679 --> 00:11:09,320
Mind the pace.

157
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:11,360
Music would make it even better.

158
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:12,919
Yang Le.

159
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:14,480
Do you play piano?

160
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:18,600
You could learn with some practice.

161
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:20,120
You're the prince.

162
00:11:20,519 --> 00:11:21,919
Playing the piano as well

163
00:11:22,279 --> 00:11:23,799
would make you more princely.

164
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:26,279
All right, class.

165
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:28,519
Let's rehearse it one last time.

166
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:29,600
Mind the emotion.

167
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:30,759
Show some feeling.

168
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:31,399
Let's begin.

169
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:38,320
Her beautiful voice

170
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:41,720
was like the rising sun.

171
00:11:42,759 --> 00:11:43,799
Beautiful voice.

172
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,240
Beautiful voice.

173
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,799
Beautiful voice.

174
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:13,639
Excuse me.

175
00:12:14,799 --> 00:12:15,559
Here for someone?

176
00:12:15,919 --> 00:12:17,279
I want to sign up for the contest.

177
00:12:19,919 --> 00:12:20,759
Su Lin.

178
00:12:21,279 --> 00:12:22,600
Did you bring your English grade?

179
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:23,679
What's your rank?

180
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:24,600
Hospitality class.

181
00:12:25,039 --> 00:12:25,559
First.

182
00:12:27,799 --> 00:12:29,120
If your grades are that good,

183
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,639
why didn't you sign up?

184
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,399
I missed the deadline.

185
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:36,279
Have you read

186
00:12:36,399 --> 00:12:37,960
Andersen's The Little Mermaid?

187
00:12:38,406 --> 00:12:38,821
Yes.

188
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,039
Read a passage.

189
00:12:40,279 --> 00:12:40,840
Relax.

190
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,960
I want to hear how you pronounce it.

191
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:46,360
This was the last evening

192
00:12:47,039 --> 00:12:49,679
that she would breathe
the same air with him

193
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:51,200
or gaze

194
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:53,519
on the starry sky and the deep sea.

195
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:54,440
And

196
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:56,960
eternal night,

197
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:00,879
without a thought or a dream,

198
00:13:01,639 --> 00:13:02,720
awaited her.

199
00:13:04,039 --> 00:13:05,320
She had no soul,

200
00:13:05,519 --> 00:13:08,440
and now she could never win one.

201
00:13:10,639 --> 00:13:11,480
Ms. Wang, come here.

202
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:12,480
Okay.

203
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,960
Ms. Wang, did you hear that?

204
00:13:17,279 --> 00:13:18,639
She knows it all by heart.

205
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:19,919
Not only that,

206
00:13:19,919 --> 00:13:20,759
even to music.

207
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:21,960
If she can,

208
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,360
then memorization clearly

209
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:24,559
isn't a problem for her.

210
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:27,440
Our team needs someone like her.

211
00:13:27,679 --> 00:13:28,360
All right.

212
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,320
Don't we still have

213
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:31,399
the role of Maid C?

214
00:13:32,519 --> 00:13:33,159
Principal Dong

215
00:13:33,279 --> 00:13:35,519
invited you from the Cultural Center

216
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,440
because we're aiming for first place.

217
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,279
Not my point.

218
00:13:38,679 --> 00:13:39,600
I mean,

219
00:13:40,399 --> 00:13:42,720
she's the perfect Little Mermaid.

220
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,200
Mr. Zhou,

221
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:45,960
I mentioned this before.

222
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,679
Ma Na's casting...

223
00:13:47,679 --> 00:13:48,320
I know.

224
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:49,679
Her father's company

225
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,639
is a major school donor.

226
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,240
But my goal

227
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:55,519
is to win this contest.

228
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:57,399
I understand.

229
00:13:57,799 --> 00:13:58,559
The problem is,

230
00:13:59,639 --> 00:14:00,879
Ma Na's role

231
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,200
was specifically arranged

232
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,559
by our principal.

233
00:14:03,799 --> 00:14:04,240
Yes.

234
00:14:04,679 --> 00:14:06,440
Our principal values these contests.

235
00:14:06,879 --> 00:14:07,320
Ms. Wang,

236
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,799
this is a provincial contest.

237
00:14:10,399 --> 00:14:11,919
Winning it earns bonus points

238
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,360
on the college entrance exam.

239
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:16,240
That's why I divided the recitation

240
00:14:16,279 --> 00:14:17,440
among several students,

241
00:14:17,919 --> 00:14:19,360
to make up for their weaknesses.

242
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:21,440
Ms. Wang,

243
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,039
to be perfectly honest,

244
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:25,399
the Little Mermaid is the lead.

245
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,200
She must know her lines cold.

246
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,440
Ma Na...

247
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:34,120
She can't even read them fluently,

248
00:14:35,039 --> 00:14:35,840
let alone memorize.

249
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,519
That simply won't work.

250
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:41,600
Then

251
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:45,200
I'll discuss it with the principal.

252
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,000
Great. Thank you, Ms. Wang.

253
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,840
I have one more tiny request.

254
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:50,480
Could you have this student
come tomorrow

255
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:53,399
and try for the Little Mermaid role?

256
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:55,759
One day only.

257
00:14:58,799 --> 00:15:00,879
All right. Mr. Zhou, she's all yours.

258
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:02,000
Thank you.

259
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:02,799
Thank you.

260
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:04,879
Come along.

261
00:15:05,919 --> 00:15:06,480
This way.

262
00:15:08,399 --> 00:15:08,879
Line up.

263
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,159
Your name?

264
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:15,440
Su Lin.

265
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:16,960
Everyone,

266
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:19,120
Ms. Wang and I have decided.

267
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,000
Tomorrow,

268
00:15:20,639 --> 00:15:22,360
Su Lin

269
00:15:22,679 --> 00:15:24,519
will try the Little Mermaid role.

270
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:29,360
Hurry up!

271
00:15:59,639 --> 00:16:00,080
Su Lin.

272
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,799
Did you miss the deadline

273
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,279
because you ran out of time?

274
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,320
I have to help at home after school.

275
00:16:10,039 --> 00:16:11,360
I can't join extracurriculars.

276
00:16:12,159 --> 00:16:13,440
It's a provincial contest.

277
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:16,080
Winning earns college entrance points.

278
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:18,720
So I still owe you thanks.

279
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,120
I overheard you

280
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,399
talking with the others.

281
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,600
That's how I found out.

282
00:16:23,679 --> 00:16:24,120
I see.

283
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,519
I'm doing it because I want college...

284
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:32,159
We should get going.

285
00:16:37,639 --> 00:16:38,360
Just let her go?

286
00:16:38,759 --> 00:16:39,320
What else?

287
00:16:39,559 --> 00:16:40,799
Beat her up before Yang Le?

288
00:17:14,599 --> 00:17:16,440
See you tomorrow at four.

289
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:20,316
(The Little Mermaid Script)

290
00:17:23,039 --> 00:17:24,000
Thank you, Mr. Zhou.

291
00:17:27,119 --> 00:17:28,759
Remember to wear white sneakers.

292
00:17:46,839 --> 00:17:47,400
Hey, sis.

293
00:17:49,359 --> 00:17:50,119
Dad bought me new clothes.

294
00:17:50,119 --> 00:17:51,039
Cool, huh?

295
00:17:59,279 --> 00:18:00,079
Come eat. Mom's waiting.

296
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:01,160
Got it.

297
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,839
It has a zipper.

298
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:16,119
Shut it.

299
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:17,319
Mom.

300
00:18:17,799 --> 00:18:18,759
We're having fish today?

301
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,400
Your dad landed a big job.

302
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:24,039
Three whole months of work.

303
00:18:25,839 --> 00:18:27,880
Don't get grease on those sleeves.

304
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:28,680
Roll them up.

305
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:30,279
Here.

306
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:32,319
Have some fish.

307
00:18:34,519 --> 00:18:35,440
Check it for bones.

308
00:18:36,119 --> 00:18:37,799
Fish will make you smarter.

309
00:18:41,039 --> 00:18:41,920
Here. Eat up.

310
00:18:44,559 --> 00:18:47,039
Fish belly is the most delicious part.

311
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:48,000
Here.

312
00:19:22,079 --> 00:19:22,480
Dad.

313
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:26,079
I need new white sneakers.

314
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,079
My old pair is too small.

315
00:19:28,319 --> 00:19:29,720
The school needs me to...

316
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:32,920
I have yet to receive my payment,

317
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:33,960
and you're spending it.

318
00:19:35,519 --> 00:19:36,400
You think our money

319
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,480
grows on trees?

320
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:38,359
Lin,

321
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:39,680
you're a girl

322
00:19:39,799 --> 00:19:41,079
and you're still growing.

323
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,480
Buy shoes too big

324
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,599
only makes your feet grow.

325
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,799
If you end up with huge feet,

326
00:19:46,559 --> 00:19:47,640
who'll ever date you?

327
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:00,640
Gu?

328
00:21:08,319 --> 00:21:09,640
Why are you still awake?

329
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:11,720
About to sleep,

330
00:21:11,839 --> 00:21:13,000
but my stomach growled.

331
00:21:13,599 --> 00:21:14,440
I'll fry two eggs,

332
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:15,759
then head to bed.

333
00:21:16,039 --> 00:21:16,759
I'll sleep better.

334
00:21:16,839 --> 00:21:17,400
I'm sorry.

335
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:18,880
We're out of sugar.

336
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:20,519
My son insisted on having

337
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:21,720
tomatoes with sugar.

338
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,960
I only just noticed.

339
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,880
I'll buy some and repay you tomorrow.

340
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,000
No need.

341
00:21:30,039 --> 00:21:30,920
The store had a sale.

342
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,519
Two bags were cheaper.

343
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:33,480
Take one.

344
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,880
(A Bag of Sugar)

345
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:36,000
I feel terrible taking it.

346
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:36,720
It's fine.

347
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:38,039
This is good sugar.

348
00:21:38,039 --> 00:21:40,119
We can rarely afford it ourselves.

349
00:21:41,039 --> 00:21:41,759
Thank you.

350
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:43,759
Only a former police officer like you

351
00:21:43,759 --> 00:21:45,559
would always be helping people.

352
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:47,640
You know,

353
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:49,559
the family who lived here before you

354
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:51,599
were awful people.

355
00:21:51,839 --> 00:21:53,039
Whenever I hung laundry,

356
00:21:53,079 --> 00:21:54,359
they'd argue with me.

357
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,559
Every single day.

358
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:58,079
Thanks again.

359
00:22:30,799 --> 00:22:31,279
Lin.

360
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,200
My pen won't write.

361
00:22:34,319 --> 00:22:34,920
Check it?

362
00:22:40,039 --> 00:22:40,519
There.

363
00:22:46,839 --> 00:22:48,319
Don't shake a pen with ink inside.

364
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:49,839
You'll get ink on yourself.

365
00:23:48,279 --> 00:23:53,319
(British Museum)

366
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:55,440
(British Museum)

367
00:23:57,079 --> 00:23:57,720
(Kitchen)

368
00:23:59,359 --> 00:24:00,119
(Kitchen)

369
00:24:00,839 --> 00:24:01,759
(Kitchen)

370
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,200
(I'm Not Sure About This One)

371
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:11,880
Mr. Gu.

372
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:13,039
All done?

373
00:24:14,640 --> 00:24:15,359
Didn't we agree

374
00:24:15,359 --> 00:24:17,039
to practice English every day?

375
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:20,000
Why didn't you record?

376
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:21,759
I just came for this.

377
00:24:22,359 --> 00:24:23,599
Ms. Du's drainpipe

378
00:24:23,799 --> 00:24:25,160
was clogged yesterday.

379
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:26,240
I worked on it all day,

380
00:24:26,559 --> 00:24:27,319
so I couldn't.

381
00:24:28,039 --> 00:24:29,359
No excuses.

382
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:31,119
We had a deal.

383
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:34,599
Record all the words from the start,

384
00:24:34,720 --> 00:24:35,880
then add the new ones.

385
00:24:36,039 --> 00:24:36,880
I'll make up for it today.

386
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:41,079
We made the rules ourselves.

387
00:24:41,359 --> 00:24:42,720
If we don't finish,

388
00:24:42,799 --> 00:24:43,799
we do it ten extra times.

389
00:24:43,920 --> 00:24:45,079
Read it all ten times?

390
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:46,519
Isn't that too much?

391
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:48,240
You're not backing out, are you?

392
00:24:48,599 --> 00:24:49,759
I have to listen ten times, too.

393
00:24:51,960 --> 00:24:53,640
All right. Your wish is my command.

394
00:24:59,799 --> 00:25:00,480
I'll do it.

395
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:01,319
You'd better go.

396
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:02,359
I'm leaving, then.

397
00:25:09,519 --> 00:25:10,119
Mr. Gu.

398
00:25:13,079 --> 00:25:14,000
I'm entering

399
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:15,559
provincial English recitation contest.

400
00:25:17,559 --> 00:25:18,000
Good.

401
00:25:20,759 --> 00:25:21,400
Good pronunciation.

402
00:25:22,279 --> 00:25:22,759
Off you go.

403
00:26:55,960 --> 00:26:57,960
Fold these clothes when they're dry.

404
00:27:01,279 --> 00:27:02,000
Oh, Lin.

405
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:05,440
Go buy two fried dough sticks.

406
00:27:06,079 --> 00:27:07,920
Your brother's been asking for them

407
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:08,960
for days now.

408
00:27:09,519 --> 00:27:10,440
Hurry and get two.

409
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:38,920
Did you do this?

410
00:27:40,279 --> 00:27:41,559
Did you ruin my shoes?

411
00:27:43,759 --> 00:27:45,200
Why are you running? Answer me!

412
00:27:45,640 --> 00:27:46,559
Was it you?

413
00:27:46,799 --> 00:27:48,599
No! I want breakfast.

414
00:27:48,640 --> 00:27:49,599
Food, now?

415
00:27:50,279 --> 00:27:51,000
Answer me.

416
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:52,440
Mom! Dad!

417
00:27:52,799 --> 00:27:54,240
My sister's trying to hit me!

418
00:28:01,400 --> 00:28:02,480
Your father's sleeping.

419
00:28:02,519 --> 00:28:03,759
Can you two keep it down?

420
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:05,519
What happened? Get up.

421
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:07,880
She hit me!

422
00:28:08,319 --> 00:28:09,440
Why did you hit him?

423
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:10,480
Let me see.

424
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,599
I didn't!

425
00:28:11,960 --> 00:28:13,839
Look what he did to my shoes.

426
00:28:14,319 --> 00:28:16,079
How am I supposed to wear
these to school now?!

427
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:17,880
What's going on?

428
00:28:18,599 --> 00:28:20,519
Why all the noise this early?

429
00:28:20,759 --> 00:28:22,400
I didn't do it on purpose!

430
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:24,240
Don't tell me it was an accident!

431
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:24,839
You

432
00:28:25,359 --> 00:28:26,000
did this?

433
00:28:26,960 --> 00:28:27,960
You little brat!

434
00:28:27,960 --> 00:28:29,240
All you do is ruin things!

435
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:31,279
- I...
- Enough! Don't hit him.

436
00:28:32,160 --> 00:28:33,920
Mom, it hurts here.

437
00:28:35,759 --> 00:28:36,559
And you!

438
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:37,759
You should watch him.

439
00:28:37,759 --> 00:28:38,920
What were you doing?

440
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:41,880
I can't even get a decent sleep.

441
00:28:42,079 --> 00:28:43,960
What did we raise you for?

442
00:28:48,599 --> 00:28:49,519
You spoiled him rotten.

443
00:28:51,759 --> 00:28:52,880
All over some stupid shoes.

444
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:54,920
You ruined my sleep.

445
00:28:55,359 --> 00:28:57,480
All you think about is school,

446
00:28:57,839 --> 00:28:59,119
and going to college.

447
00:28:59,599 --> 00:29:01,440
You obsess over English all day.

448
00:29:01,799 --> 00:29:02,880
Why learn that stuff?

449
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:04,680
What good will it do?

450
00:29:06,799 --> 00:29:08,559
You're all ungrateful.

451
00:29:09,319 --> 00:29:10,960
I work from dawn to dusk.

452
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:12,680
Everything costs money.

453
00:29:13,400 --> 00:29:14,519
Just quit school.

454
00:29:14,839 --> 00:29:16,640
Get home and work!

455
00:29:17,400 --> 00:29:18,039
Wait.

456
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:19,960
You're not having breakfast?

457
00:29:20,400 --> 00:29:21,440
How could I eat now?

458
00:29:21,480 --> 00:29:22,920
I'm so full of anger.

459
00:29:23,279 --> 00:29:25,039
Then take two steamed buns.

460
00:29:25,039 --> 00:29:25,839
Wait!

461
00:29:26,559 --> 00:29:27,400
Wait!

462
00:29:41,079 --> 00:29:43,119
(Blue Rainstorm Alert Issued.)

463
00:29:43,359 --> 00:29:43,799
(Forecast:)

464
00:29:43,839 --> 00:29:46,279
(from 8:00 to 24:00 on the 23rd,)

465
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:47,759
(heavy to torrential rain in our city,)

466
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,400
(with downpours in some areas.)

467
00:29:49,720 --> 00:29:51,960
(Residents should prepare for rain.)

468
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:54,599
(The government and agencies)

469
00:29:54,599 --> 00:29:56,720
(will enact emergency measures.)

470
00:29:57,079 --> 00:29:58,000
Off to school?

471
00:29:59,559 --> 00:30:00,079
Mr. Gu.

472
00:30:05,079 --> 00:30:05,799
What is it now?

473
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:10,200
They're forecasting heavy rain.

474
00:30:10,599 --> 00:30:11,240
Got an umbrella?

475
00:30:13,279 --> 00:30:13,839
Wait here.

476
00:30:25,329 --> 00:30:28,284
(Chaobei Vocational High School)

477
00:30:30,240 --> 00:30:30,640
Brother.

478
00:30:44,720 --> 00:30:45,680
Go on to school.

479
00:30:47,799 --> 00:30:48,599
Dad promised you,

480
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:49,880
and I'll keep it.

481
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:51,960
You'll still lead the recitation team.

482
00:30:52,200 --> 00:30:53,640
It's the Little Mermaid.

483
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:54,960
That's the role I want.

484
00:30:54,960 --> 00:30:56,279
She's called the Little Mermaid.

485
00:30:56,400 --> 00:30:57,839
Right. The Little Mermaid.

486
00:30:58,319 --> 00:30:59,240
Of course it'll be you.

487
00:30:59,359 --> 00:31:00,559
No one else could do it.

488
00:31:02,119 --> 00:31:03,400
Go on. You'll be late.

489
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:05,359
Drink water.

490
00:31:06,839 --> 00:31:07,279
Na!

491
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:09,279
Your jacket!

492
00:31:10,519 --> 00:31:11,720
You forgot it.

493
00:31:12,039 --> 00:31:13,559
Here. Put it on. Quick.

494
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:15,519
I bought cakes for you

495
00:31:15,519 --> 00:31:17,079
and your friends tonight,

496
00:31:17,240 --> 00:31:18,359
from the new Haolilai.

497
00:31:19,279 --> 00:31:21,160
Your study abroad plans are nearly set.

498
00:31:21,359 --> 00:31:22,079
No matter what,

499
00:31:22,079 --> 00:31:23,160
you must master English.

500
00:31:23,920 --> 00:31:24,359
Okay.

501
00:31:26,039 --> 00:31:27,119
Make sure you have lunch.

502
00:31:27,319 --> 00:31:28,359
Don't skip it.

503
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:40,559
You even restyled your shoes

504
00:31:40,559 --> 00:31:42,039
to play the Little Mermaid?

505
00:31:42,279 --> 00:31:43,319
Very ocean-inspired.

506
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:45,519
And you add some raised patterns.

507
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:46,960
Na, look at her feet.

508
00:31:47,519 --> 00:31:48,720
Such an attention-seeker.

509
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:50,920
Su Lin, walk for us.

510
00:31:51,799 --> 00:31:53,079
Go on. Walk.

511
00:31:55,119 --> 00:31:56,079
Time to line up.

512
00:31:59,920 --> 00:32:01,440
Come on. The teacher called us.

513
00:32:02,799 --> 00:32:03,359
Everyone,

514
00:32:04,079 --> 00:32:05,039
I have an announcement.

515
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:07,039
For various reasons,

516
00:32:08,279 --> 00:32:09,480
we've decided

517
00:32:09,880 --> 00:32:12,039
Ma Na will remain the Little Mermaid.

518
00:32:12,440 --> 00:32:13,839
Sorry about that.

519
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:16,200
Then what about Su Lin?

520
00:32:16,440 --> 00:32:17,799
Her English is excellent,

521
00:32:17,920 --> 00:32:19,039
so she'll stay in the play.

522
00:32:19,519 --> 00:32:20,680
She'll play Maid C.

523
00:32:21,680 --> 00:32:22,640
Maid C?

524
00:32:22,759 --> 00:32:24,079
How impressive, Su Lin.

525
00:32:24,119 --> 00:32:25,440
- Let's applaud her.
- Maid C.

526
00:32:25,440 --> 00:32:26,119
Congratulations.

527
00:32:26,119 --> 00:32:26,880
Congratulations!

528
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:28,200
Amazing.

529
00:32:28,519 --> 00:32:29,079
All right.

530
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:30,640
Start rehearsing

531
00:32:30,640 --> 00:32:31,440
with Mr. Zhou.

532
00:32:31,920 --> 00:32:32,960
Every day, he

533
00:32:33,079 --> 00:32:34,759
finishes work at the Cultural Center

534
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:36,400
and comes here to work overtime.

535
00:32:36,599 --> 00:32:38,359
We owe his first place, don't we?

536
00:32:38,920 --> 00:32:40,759
Sorry.

537
00:32:40,839 --> 00:32:41,880
Mr. Zhou.

538
00:32:42,960 --> 00:32:44,079
All right. Let's begin.

539
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,400
Bye-bye, Maid C.

540
00:32:49,240 --> 00:32:50,759
Here comes the Little Mermaid.

541
00:32:51,880 --> 00:32:54,119
I told you the role would be mine.

542
00:32:54,279 --> 00:32:55,119
Of course.

543
00:32:55,279 --> 00:32:56,720
Just look who your father is.

544
00:32:58,920 --> 00:32:59,720
Thank you.

545
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:06,319
Bathroom.

546
00:33:06,759 --> 00:33:07,960
Bathroom.

547
00:33:09,880 --> 00:33:10,640
Bedroom.

548
00:33:11,680 --> 00:33:12,960
Bedroom.

549
00:33:14,920 --> 00:33:15,519
Home.

550
00:33:16,519 --> 00:33:17,240
Home.

551
00:33:18,759 --> 00:33:19,440
All /m/.

552
00:33:21,519 --> 00:33:23,000
Puh-tay-toe.

553
00:33:23,559 --> 00:33:24,759
Potato, Lin.

554
00:33:25,119 --> 00:33:26,759
I'm not sure about the English.

555
00:33:27,079 --> 00:33:28,559
Teach me one more time.

556
00:33:30,279 --> 00:33:30,920
Na.

557
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:31,960
Yours.

558
00:33:32,920 --> 00:33:34,680
Who picked this? It's hideous.

559
00:33:35,519 --> 00:33:36,519
I think it's okay.

560
00:33:38,079 --> 00:33:39,960
Put this on Su Lin later.

561
00:33:40,519 --> 00:33:42,039
Let's see what a penniless

562
00:33:42,039 --> 00:33:42,799
mermaid looks like.

563
00:33:48,519 --> 00:33:49,119
Let go of me!

564
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:49,799
Don't try anything.

565
00:33:50,039 --> 00:33:51,200
Where are you taking me?

566
00:33:51,279 --> 00:33:51,839
Get inside.

567
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:52,839
I won't go in.

568
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:53,319
Get in!

569
00:33:53,319 --> 00:33:54,079
Let me go!

570
00:33:56,920 --> 00:33:59,200
(Dressing Room)
So you're the perfect Little Mermaid?

571
00:33:59,640 --> 00:34:01,240
Let's see what makes you so perfect.

572
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:05,799
Put it on.

573
00:34:06,359 --> 00:34:07,200
I said no.

574
00:34:07,599 --> 00:34:08,800
Say it again. Put it on.

575
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:09,239
No.

576
00:34:09,440 --> 00:34:10,480
You won't?

577
00:34:10,719 --> 00:34:11,760
Is that right?

578
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:14,519
I'll do it myself!

579
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:17,719
I'll put it on.

580
00:34:28,960 --> 00:34:29,519
Yang Le.

581
00:34:36,039 --> 00:34:37,119
Come on. Outside.

582
00:34:42,440 --> 00:34:43,199
You?

583
00:34:43,760 --> 00:34:45,039
The Little Mermaid?

584
00:34:45,639 --> 00:34:46,440
As if.

585
00:34:48,039 --> 00:34:51,400
"There it is for you," said the witch.

586
00:34:53,159 --> 00:34:55,039
Then she cut out

587
00:34:55,800 --> 00:34:56,639
the mermaid's tongue,

588
00:34:56,840 --> 00:34:57,920
so that she

589
00:34:59,280 --> 00:35:01,599
would never again speak or sing.

590
00:35:05,159 --> 00:35:06,880
That's what you are doing now.

591
00:35:10,960 --> 00:35:11,760
So, am I

592
00:35:12,880 --> 00:35:13,320
worthy now?

593
00:35:13,800 --> 00:35:14,800
What a load of nonsense.

594
00:35:14,880 --> 00:35:15,480
Ma Na.

595
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:18,119
She really is the best choice.

596
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:19,199
Stop this.

597
00:35:23,039 --> 00:35:23,800
Su Lin.

598
00:35:24,639 --> 00:35:26,000
Why did you steal my dress?

599
00:35:26,639 --> 00:35:27,960
Give it back right now.

600
00:35:28,199 --> 00:35:29,280
I didn't steal it.

601
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,400
Then what's that?

602
00:35:31,079 --> 00:35:31,760
Exactly.

603
00:35:31,880 --> 00:35:32,960
You stole her dress

604
00:35:32,960 --> 00:35:34,000
and put it on?

605
00:35:34,679 --> 00:35:36,039
You three forced me to wear it.

606
00:35:36,079 --> 00:35:36,960
I saw the whole thing.

607
00:35:37,360 --> 00:35:38,440
You stole it.

608
00:35:38,480 --> 00:35:40,119
Take it off and give it back.

609
00:35:40,559 --> 00:35:41,760
Enjoy wearing stolen clothes?

610
00:35:42,159 --> 00:35:42,840
Su Lin.

611
00:35:44,840 --> 00:35:45,519
We'll remove it.

612
00:35:46,079 --> 00:35:46,639
Come on.

613
00:35:48,320 --> 00:35:50,480
Song Shuang! Zhao Lingling! Stop!

614
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:52,079
What? Want to join her?

615
00:35:52,119 --> 00:35:53,000
I said stop!

616
00:35:53,239 --> 00:35:53,599
Let go.

617
00:35:53,599 --> 00:35:54,800
Stop it! Do you hear me?

618
00:35:55,480 --> 00:35:57,000
Did you hear me? Stop!

619
00:35:57,119 --> 00:35:58,159
You want to hit us now?

620
00:35:58,280 --> 00:35:58,880
Let go!

621
00:35:59,039 --> 00:35:59,599
Move!

622
00:35:59,639 --> 00:36:00,800
Song Shuang, let go!

623
00:36:00,880 --> 00:36:01,679
Hands off! Let go!

624
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:02,519
What's going on?

625
00:36:02,719 --> 00:36:04,519
Ms. Wang, Yang Le hit us.

626
00:36:04,719 --> 00:36:05,679
What are you doing?

627
00:36:11,320 --> 00:36:12,239
School's over.

628
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:13,880
Why are you causing trouble here?

629
00:36:15,719 --> 00:36:16,360
Ms. Wang.

630
00:36:17,960 --> 00:36:18,960
She stole my dress.

631
00:36:20,039 --> 00:36:20,960
I didn't.

632
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:23,679
That's a lie.

633
00:36:23,840 --> 00:36:25,039
I have two witnesses.

634
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:27,199
The three of you forced me to wear it.

635
00:36:28,960 --> 00:36:30,119
Let's ask the principal.

636
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:31,440
He can call my father.

637
00:36:32,760 --> 00:36:34,119
Let's see if they believe you

638
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:35,840
or me.

639
00:36:36,079 --> 00:36:37,000
Enough of this.

640
00:36:37,800 --> 00:36:38,440
All of you, go.

641
00:36:39,119 --> 00:36:40,079
Don't you have homework?

642
00:36:46,039 --> 00:36:46,559
Su Lin.

643
00:36:47,199 --> 00:36:47,719
You okay?

644
00:36:48,079 --> 00:36:48,679
Are you hurt?

645
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:51,519
Yang Le.

646
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,119
Why did you help her?

647
00:36:54,400 --> 00:36:56,079
What she said in English was right.

648
00:36:57,320 --> 00:36:58,960
I was only telling the truth.

649
00:36:59,760 --> 00:37:00,920
What does that mean?

650
00:37:01,639 --> 00:37:02,920
What did she mean?

651
00:37:03,519 --> 00:37:04,840
What did that part of English mean?

652
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:20,880
Hurry up.

653
00:37:24,920 --> 00:37:25,920
- Look out!
- Na!

654
00:37:26,039 --> 00:37:26,440
Slow down!

655
00:37:56,480 --> 00:37:57,519
What do you want from me?

656
00:38:00,960 --> 00:38:02,159
What did you just call me?

657
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:06,719
Take her inside.

658
00:38:12,360 --> 00:38:14,320
Help! Somebody help!

659
00:38:15,199 --> 00:38:15,840
Help!

660
00:38:16,199 --> 00:38:17,159
You like running, huh?

661
00:38:17,559 --> 00:38:19,079
Go on, run!

662
00:38:19,280 --> 00:38:21,280
Run! Keep running!

663
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:22,119
I'll teach you!

664
00:38:22,559 --> 00:38:23,239
Get off me!

665
00:38:25,719 --> 00:38:26,199
Get lost!

666
00:38:33,519 --> 00:38:34,039
Get her!

667
00:38:35,639 --> 00:38:36,239
You fell.

668
00:38:37,280 --> 00:38:37,840
Done?

669
00:38:38,599 --> 00:38:39,280
Back off?

670
00:38:40,320 --> 00:38:41,119
Get up and play.

671
00:38:44,360 --> 00:38:45,960
Stay back!

672
00:38:47,440 --> 00:38:48,519
A compass?

673
00:38:49,440 --> 00:38:50,360
She's got a weapon.

674
00:38:51,039 --> 00:38:52,519
Go on. Stab me.

675
00:38:53,159 --> 00:38:54,960
Stay back!

676
00:38:55,360 --> 00:38:56,280
Don't come any closer!

677
00:38:57,159 --> 00:38:58,880
Please, don't come any closer.

678
00:39:01,079 --> 00:39:02,280
Look at you, Su Lin.

679
00:39:02,480 --> 00:39:03,480
A weapon? Seriously?

680
00:39:03,639 --> 00:39:05,000
Stay away from me!

681
00:39:05,239 --> 00:39:06,679
Stay away!

682
00:39:08,760 --> 00:39:09,760
Don't come any closer!

683
00:39:20,840 --> 00:39:22,239
What are you looking at? Get lost!

684
00:39:37,760 --> 00:39:38,800
Now,

685
00:39:39,039 --> 00:39:39,639
let's settle

686
00:39:39,639 --> 00:39:40,679
the score between us.

687
00:39:40,800 --> 00:39:42,079
Trying to take your role

688
00:39:42,800 --> 00:39:43,679
was my fault.

689
00:39:44,559 --> 00:39:45,760
I didn't want to upstage you.

690
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:47,840
I only wanted the bonus points.

691
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:49,199
Upstage me?

692
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:50,760
As if you could.

693
00:39:51,320 --> 00:39:52,079
Stay back!

694
00:39:52,360 --> 00:39:53,199
Don't come closer!

695
00:39:53,239 --> 00:39:54,239
You think I didn't know

696
00:39:54,239 --> 00:39:55,320
you called me the witch?

697
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:56,440
Come on.

698
00:39:56,719 --> 00:39:57,639
You're so tough.

699
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:58,320
Stab me.

700
00:39:58,599 --> 00:39:59,000
Come on.

701
00:39:59,280 --> 00:39:59,880
Show me.

702
00:40:00,039 --> 00:40:00,719
Stab me.

703
00:40:00,880 --> 00:40:01,360
Come on!

704
00:40:01,519 --> 00:40:02,280
Right here!

705
00:40:16,438 --> 00:40:19,076
=Ren Yu=
(Next Time...)

706
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:22,599
Su Lin!

707
00:40:23,760 --> 00:40:24,199
Su Lin!

708
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:26,000
No answer.

709
00:40:26,760 --> 00:40:27,960
Did the fall kill her?

710
00:40:29,239 --> 00:40:30,760
Today, a woman's body

711
00:40:31,159 --> 00:40:32,880
floated out of the Weihong Canal.

712
00:40:33,320 --> 00:40:33,920
Honey.

713
00:40:34,559 --> 00:40:36,400
Lin didn't come home all night.

714
00:40:39,320 --> 00:40:40,679
When her family sees she's gone,

715
00:40:40,719 --> 00:40:42,000
they'll call the police.

716
00:40:42,639 --> 00:40:44,280
You can't cover this up.

717
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:47,119
Then stop them from calling.

718
00:41:06,042 --> 00:41:09,002
♪A faint heartbeat♪

719
00:41:09,002 --> 00:41:11,322
♪Scales drifting♪

720
00:41:11,977 --> 00:41:14,118
♪In dark brine♪

721
00:41:14,118 --> 00:41:16,967
♪Scorched gills appear♪

722
00:41:17,889 --> 00:41:20,769
♪An empty shell♪

723
00:41:20,769 --> 00:41:23,249
♪A banished soul♪

724
00:41:23,809 --> 00:41:25,816
♪Moonlight♪

725
00:41:25,816 --> 00:41:28,776
♪Splinters into shards♪

726
00:41:29,709 --> 00:41:32,669
♪Don't look back, don't look back♪

727
00:41:35,672 --> 00:41:38,443
♪Dust drifts♪

728
00:41:38,443 --> 00:41:40,872
♪Through the silent abyss♪

729
00:41:41,556 --> 00:41:44,516
♪Don't look back, don't look back♪

730
00:41:47,335 --> 00:41:50,215
♪Tides recede♪

731
00:41:50,501 --> 00:41:52,741
♪We grow in the dark♪

732
00:42:17,124 --> 00:42:20,084
♪Don't look back, don't look back♪

733
00:42:23,086 --> 00:42:25,967
♪Memories buried♪

734
00:42:25,967 --> 00:42:28,287
♪Sorrow forgotten♪

735
00:42:28,955 --> 00:42:31,727
♪Swim ahead, swim ahead♪

736
00:42:34,828 --> 00:42:37,468
♪Above the deep sea♪

737
00:42:37,468 --> 00:42:40,108
♪We are scars swimming upstream♪

738
00:43:04,485 --> 00:43:07,365
♪Don't look back, don't look back♪

739
00:43:10,422 --> 00:43:13,222
♪Deep-sea wounds♪

740
00:43:13,222 --> 00:43:15,862
♪We swim upstream♪
